    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Constitutional bodies derive their authority and powers directly from the Constitution of India.",
        "Statutory bodies are created by an Act of Parliament or State Legislature.",
        "Executive bodies are established through a cabinet resolution without parliamentary legislation.",
        "Modifying the structure or powers of a constitutional body requires a constitutional amendment under Article 368."
      ],
      "id": "tkaz1l3"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Questions frequently test the distinction between Constitutional, Statutory, and Executive bodies.",
        "Memorize key constitutional articles establishing bodies such as CAG (Art. 148), UPSC (Art. 315), and Election Commission (Art. 324).",
        "Note that bodies like NITI Aayog and CVC originated via executive resolution and statute respectively, not constitutional provision."
      ],
